{
  "date": "2026-10-25",
  "scope": "Actual Coordinator task-target parsing and its correspondence through independent successful JSON interpretations and queue WAL recovery. Complete task-state/cache/admission and business-fold refinement remain open.",
  "properties": {
    "queue_event::{string_field,array_field,collect,prepare}": "Exact complete ordered ID lists for Submitted/Leased row IDs, Epoch revoked IDs, Expired/Failed IDs, Cancelled/Yielded/TaskProgress direct IDs and Completed receipt task ID. Duplicates and order are preserved; invalid target fields are rejected and well-shaped inputs cannot be rejected arbitrarily. Non-task event types yield an empty list and remain subject to later business validation.",
    "queue_event_equivalence::{field_equal,identity_equal,array_equal,array_targets_equal,targets_equal}": "Finite-depth Value observations preserve the exact selected type and ordered task targets, including malformed-target rejection. This is not representation equality or complete numeric/task semantics.",
    "queue_event_equivalence::{parsed_targets_equal,preparations_equal,transaction_targets_equal}": "Successful parses of the same raw JSON select identical targets; actual prepared outputs preserve target characters and order; transaction positions are preserved.",
    "journal_equivalence::{recovered_frame_targets,recovered_history_targets}": "Composes accepted-frame encoding, exact byte replay and successful Value parsing with task-target correspondence. The same valid frame or arbitrary finite encoded history yields the same ordered targets at each transaction/event position."
  },
  "runtime_changes": "Coordinator::apply calls the shared parser before invalidating pending/leased/usage indexes. The parser uses the same borrowed str indexing primitive beneath serde_json Value indexing, preserving tree lookup without allocating lookup keys or scanning whole objects. The output remains one ID vector and copied IDs, now reserving the known list length. Existing native error categories/messages and subsequent business branches are retained. No new I/O, format or public API change; no measured zero-overhead claim and no newly demonstrated production defect.",
  "boundaries": [
    "The single added trusted library primitive is <str as serde_json::value::Index>::index_into. Its contract returns the exact named field, or None for absent/nonobject fields. The pinned implementation was inspected and delegates to Map::get; the runner permits precisely this additional method, with no admitted straw body.",
    "ENV-JSON-LIBRARY and ENV-JSON-VALUE-CONSISTENCY retain trusted standard-library/parser/clone behavior. Same-raw interpretation does not assert parser acceptance, allocation success, arbitrary custom Deserialize determinism or full floating-point mathematical semantics.",
    "Target parsing does not validate remaining event business fields, authorize unknown event kinds, prove stale attempt/epoch rejection, or establish that all subsequent task/reader/deadline/scheduling-cache updates are correct. Non-task events deliberately produce no task targets; unknown types are still rejected by the native business dispatcher.",
    "Full Coordinator ordered business replay, native run/File/lock/prefix binding, cross-log ownership, GC and crashed-writer retirement remain unfinished. Existing narrower metadata/request/WAL proofs are retained without claiming complete composition."
  ],
